BEGIN_TEXT
Every station the radio has heard calling or sounding, the most recent
first: when it was last heard, on which channel, how often in the last
day and in all, on how many channels, and its best SINAD (in dB: higher
is cleaner). A good recent SINAD on a channel means that channel is
likely to work for a call to that station now.

Favourites are starred, with the name the box knows them by. A favourite
not heard yet is listed at the end. The favourites list comes with the
box (favourites.txt); it isn't typed here.

The figures come from the link quality database when the box keeps one,
and from the recent calls otherwise: the screen says which.
END
